<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center;">Facts</h1>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p><strong>Important Specifics You Should Know About The Lindenwoods:</strong></p>
    <p>Nature: Two coordinate Colleges, one for men, the other for women, sharing courses, faculty and facilities.</p>
    <p>Location: St. Charles, Missouri, 22 miles northwest of downtown St. Louis, 15 minutes from St. Louis' International Airport.</p>
    <p>Founding: Lindenwood College (women), 1827, Lindenwood II (men), 1969.</p>
    <p>Enrollment: Approximately <span data-field="enrollment_number">{{ enrollment_number }}</span> women, <span data-field="enrollment_number">{{ enrollment_number }}</span> men.</p>
    <p>Faculty: <span data-field="faculty_count">{{ faculty_count }}</span> Full-Time, including <span data-field="faculty_with_phd">{{ faculty_with_phd }}</span> with Ph.D. degrees.</p>
    <p>Degrees: Bachelor of arts, bachelor of science, bachelor of fine arts, bachelor of music, bachelor of music education, master of arts, master of science, and doctoral degrees in various fields.</p>
    <p>Special Features: Independent study; graduate school preparation; off-campus study in U.S. and abroad; cooperative programs with other colleges and universities; internships in broadcasting, advertising, business, art museum management, commercial art, television, industrial mathematics, health sciences and hospital administration; career-oriented liberal arts programs in communications, computer programming, mental health, medical technology, urban planning; pre-professional training in medicine, law, and veterinary medicine; private music instruction with members of St. Louis Symphony; campus school for nursery and kindergarten students; physical education with emphasis on horsemanship, recreation and theater education; January Term on-campus and off campus. Cooperative Three-Two Plan leading to Bachelor of Science in Engineering.</p>
    <p>Library: <span data-field="library_volumes">{{ library_volumes }}</span> volumes, <span data-field="library_periodicals">{{ library_periodicals }}</span> periodicals; capability for <span data-field="library_volumes_capacity">{{ library_volumes_capacity }}</span> volumes; other resources available include art history slide library and black studies media bank.</p>
    <p>Housing: Five residence halls for women and two for men; unmarried students live on campus.</p>
    <p>Athletics: Intercollegiate field hockey, tennis and basketball for women; intercollegiate soccer, tennis and basketball for men.</p>
    <p>Activities and Publications: Student-produced and student-written plays, year-round community radio station (KCLC-AM) and a campus station (KCLC-AM), a student newspaper (The Griffin) and a yearbook (The Leaves); student orchestra, choir, annual open hose show.</p>
    <p>Organizations: Special-interest groups including: Alpha Lambda Delta (freshman women honorary), Phi Sigma Tau (philosophy honorary), Alpha Epsilon Rho (broadcasting), Alpha Psi Omega (drama), Eta Sigma Pi (classics), Mu Phi Epsilon (music), Pi Mu Epsilon (mathematics), Alpha Sigma Tau (senior scholastic), Linden Scroll (honorary service for senior women), Student Artist Guild, Triangle Club (science), Beta Chi (riding), Creative Dance Group, Lambda Alpha Rho (sports), The Poetry Society, El Club de la Amistad (Spanish), The Student Interfaith Network, National Student Education Association.</p>
    <p>1973-74 Tuition — <span data-field="tuition_amount">{{ tuition_amount }}</span>; room and board—<span data-field="board_amount">{{ board_amount }}</span>; student activity fee <span data-field="activity_fee">{{ activity_fee }}</span>; health fee for resident students <span data-field="health_fee">{{ health_fee }}</span> (tuition and fees subject to change for 1974-75).</p>
  </div>

